sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch01-11> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Simple programs can reproduce many features of biological organisms and appear to capture essential mechanisms by which genetic programs generate observed biological forms, enabling new models and general abstract theories in biology.";
    dc:type "model-of-nature";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Simple programs capture how genetic programs generate biological forms";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 1, “The Foundations for a New Kind of Science”; section “Relations to Other Areas” (from p. 7), p. 9. Scope: biological morphogenesis and pigmentation patterns"
}
